        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7736245?v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><h2 dir="auto">Paper Title: SneakySnake: A Fast and Accurate Universal Genome Pre-Alignment Filter for CPUs, GPUs, and FPGAs</h2>
<h3 dir="auto">Paper Year: 2019</h3>
<h2 dir="auto">Paper Title: Shouji: a fast and efficient pre-alignment filter for sequence alignment</h2>
<h3 dir="auto">Paper Year: 2019</h3>
<h2 dir="auto">Paper Title: Shifted Hamming distance: a fast and accurate SIMD-friendly filter to accelerate alignment verification in read mapping</h2>
<h3 dir="auto">Paper Year: 2015</h3>
<h3 dir="auto">Reasons for including papers</h3>
<p dir="auto">In genomic sequence analysis, it’s crucial to develop a fast and accurate filter that can rapidly and efficiently detect error-abundant string pairs and remove them from consideration before more computationally expensive methods are used, These papers show very good work in approaching a solution, That would help in answering the question (How can we accelerate sequence variant analysis for COVID-19 genomes?) as well.</p>]]></content>
